      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When a Black colleague is consistently overlooked for high-profile projects, it's often framed as them \"not being the right fit\" or \"lacking the necessary executive presence.\" Another subtle jab is when an Asian colleague's technical expertise is praised, but their ideas are then dismissed as \"too aggressive\" or \"not collaborative enough.\" You might also see white colleagues being praised for being \"a natural leader,\" while minority colleagues are told they need to be \"more assertive\" to be seen as leaders. These veiled critiques are designed to reinforce existing biases about who belongs in power.",
