      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For East Asian individuals, the stereotype of being \"highly analytical\" often manifests in feedback that praises meticulousness but critiques \"lacking big-picture vision,\" suggesting they are too detail-oriented to lead. Hispanic or Latinx individuals might be subtly pigeonholed into \"support roles,\" with feedback focusing heavily on their \"teamwork\" or \"cultural fit\" rather than strategic impact. Black professionals are frequently subjected to the \"aggressive\" stereotype; their strong opinions are framed as \"confrontational\" in reviews, even when they are simply advocating for necessary change. These coded criticisms are how systemic bias hides in plain sight.",
